1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Remove Element — LeetCode 27

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,750
Problem: remove every occurrence of val from nums, in place, and return k — how many remain.

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:09,800
Example: nums = [3, 2, 2, 3], val = 3

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:15,100
Result: k = 2, nums = [2, 2, …]; the rest is ignored

5
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:20,450
Hint: don't erase — overwrite nums with the keepers, left to right

6
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:26,900
Approach: two pointers — f (fast) reads every element, s (slow) marks the next write slot

7
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:31,900
Start: nums = [3, 2, 2, 3], val = 3; f and s both begin at 0

8
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:34,300
f = 0: nums[0] = 3

9
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,550
3 = val → skip; s stays

10
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:39,950
f = 1: nums[1] = 2

11
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:44,600
2 ≠ val → write it into slot s = 0

12
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:47,000
f = 2: nums[2] = 2

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,650
2 ≠ val → write it into slot s = 1

14
00:00:51,650 --> 00:00:54,050
f = 3: nums[3] = 3

15
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:57,350
3 = val → skip

16
00:00:57,350 --> 00:01:01,950
Loop ends → k = s = 2

17
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:05,850
The first k = 2 elements are the answer. Time O(n), space O(1)

18
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:13,600
